  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the key uncertainty is whether a full multimodal pipeline with strong encoders and expressive aggregation can achieve high validation accuracy. Config_008 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, concat fusion) tests the most capable combination of encoders with a standard, well-understood fusion strategy. This serves as a strong baseline: if it performs well, subsequent experiments can ablate components (e.g., swap fusion to weighted, change encoder, drop to singleprofile) to identify what drives performance; if it underperforms, we learn that complexity or a specific component is the bottleneck. Choosing the highest-capacity multimodal setup first maximizes the chance of establishing a high accuracy floor early in the budget, while the transformer aggregation and concat fusion keep the design interpretable for follow-up ablations."
}

